_publ_section_exptl_refinement
;
The powder pattern was indexed in a centered monoclinic cell. Transformation
to the standard setting and analysis of the systematic absences gave C 2/c
(No. 15). Fifty-five resolved lines through 64 degrees 2theta were reproduced
with an RMS position residual of approximately 0.005 degrees; the de Wolff
M20 figure of merit for the equivalent I-centered setting was approximately
210. Atomic coordinates were obtained by whole-pattern intensity fitting with
one crystallographically independent carbonate group. Carbonate geometry was
restrained during the powder-only coordinate refinement. The resulting C-O
distances are 1.278-1.281 angstrom; Er is eight-coordinate with Er-O distances
of 2.310-2.484 angstrom. Isotropic displacement parameters are nominal rather
than independently determined from this powder pattern.
;
